Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:07.640
I received a very interesting email from a
neuroscientist this week, and this neuroscientist

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:14.150
said, you know, David, you should just look
at the verbal symptoms of schizophrenia rather

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.180
than dementia or drug abuse to explain Donald
Trump's behavior.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.760
And I want to dig right into this now.

00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.420
Let me put the disclaimer right out there.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:24.080
I am not a neuroscientist.

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.210
I am not coming up with any of this stuff.

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:28.410
And I am not diagnosing Trump with anything.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:31.880
What I'm doing is pointing out we've been
looking at Trump's brain glitches.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:36.810
His speech patterns, his bizarre behavior,
his walking away from his limo when it was

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.530
right in front of him, his not seeing Rudy
Giuliani, when Rudy Giuliani was right in

00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:44.920
front of him, talking about the oranges of
an investigation.

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:46.899
Half Saffa hide all of that stuff.

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:47.899
Right.

00:00:47.899 --> 00:00:52.000
We have heard from professionals who say it's
cognitive decline.

00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:55.250
We've heard from professionals who say it's
dementia.

00:00:55.250 --> 00:00:58.540
We've heard it could be a side effect of medication,
could be drug abuse.

00:00:58.540 --> 00:01:00.610
A lot of different ideas.

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:05.740
A neuroscientist wrote to me and said, David,
look at the language disturbances that are

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.830
outlined in schizophrenia and just see what
you think.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:10.140
So I did it.

00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:12.630
Peer Review Journal article from this year.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.550
Journal is called Current Opinions on Psychiatry.

00:01:15.550 --> 00:01:19.220
The article is called Anomalies or Anomalies.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:21.310
Both are valid pronunciations.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:25.450
Anomalies in language is a biomarker for schizophrenia.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:31.130
And it says that impaired verbal communication
is one of the key diagnostic features of schizophrenia

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.880
spectrum disorders.

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:34.660
And it lists the following traits.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:41.200
And I have to tell you, Trump does seem to
experience every single one of these difficulties

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.590
with lexical selection and retrieval.

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:50.909
Trump has that issue, disturbances in priming
and reduced syntactic priming.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:57.970
Trump has that reduced Proactiv inhibition
difficulties with coherant lead generating

00:01:57.970 --> 00:01:59.000
a narrative.

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:06.430
Trump can't maintain a coherent narrative
when he speaks using neologisms word approximation,

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:14.419
disturbances in cohesion, vague references,
missing information and confused references.

00:02:14.419 --> 00:02:22.139
It's like it's describing Trump speech sentences
with reduced syntactic complexity, less dependance

00:02:22.139 --> 00:02:26.680
and embedded clauses and use fewer connective
markers.

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.599
That is Donald Trump's simplistic, childish
speech described to a T. Compared with normal

00:02:33.599 --> 00:02:40.950
speech, the speech of those experiencing schizophrenia
contains more hesitations, pauses and longer

00:02:40.950 --> 00:02:42.079
pauses.

00:02:42.079 --> 00:02:43.590
That's Trump.

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:47.449
Intonation is flat and monotonous.

00:02:47.449 --> 00:02:48.449
That is Trump.

00:02:48.449 --> 00:02:52.739
We've actually talked about, you know, we
say when when Trump talks about the number

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:59.409
of deaths and cases and the tragedy and suffering
of Corona virus, we notice he seems to completely

00:02:59.409 --> 00:03:01.260
lack empathy.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:09.279
It also interpreted differently could be what
the biomarkers, the verbal biomarkers of schizophrenia

00:03:09.279 --> 00:03:13.739
describe as a flat, monotonous intonation.

00:03:13.739 --> 00:03:17.219
So I'm not bringing this to you as a diagnosis.

00:03:17.219 --> 00:03:18.889
I am not coming up with this.

00:03:18.889 --> 00:03:23.310
What I'm telling you, as a neuroscientist
